# Project open / cold start (mandatory)

Living docs: [`docs/terminals.md`](../../docs/terminals.md) (Persistence →
Project open / cold start),
[`openspec/specs/terminals/projects/spec.md`](../../openspec/specs/terminals/projects/spec.md).

When opening or restoring a Project (File → Projects or last Project on
startup), **same on Linux and Windows**:

1. **Terminal tab** — every restored **live** TERMINALS session selects the
   primary Terminal tab (`active_view == 0`), even if YAML saved a filter tab.
   Do **not** leave the user on an empty filter tab after open.
2. **Manual Start** — live Programs stay **stopped**. A saved `command` does
   **not** spawn a PTY until the user presses Start on the TERMINALS row.
   Blank live terminals do **not** spawn a shell until the user types or
   explicitly Starts. Do **not** auto-start an interactive shell for Programs
   that have a saved command.
3. **FILES** — file sessions MAY begin load on open (existing FILES behavior).
   Do **not** auto-spawn a process/PTY for live Programs.
4. Empty viewport “Press Start” / type-to-open hints **are** the open path
   for stopped Programs (`EMPTY_TERMINAL_TAB_STOPPED`).
5. **CLI launch** (`noviewlog-slint -- cmd …` / `finish_startup` with a
   process or log-file launch) MAY start that one-shot command. Restoring the
   last Project on startup MUST NOT auto-start.

Do not “fix” Project open by restoring the last filter tab, and do **not**
reintroduce auto-start of saved process commands on open.
